WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.112 --> 00:00:01.890
(soft knocking)

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.330
- [Zelda] Look who's here.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.840
- Hi, Zelda, how you doing?

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.920
- I never knew there was
a school in the building.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.830
I got a note one day to show up,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.857
and I loved it from the moment we began.

00:00:13.857 --> 00:00:17.357
(soft lighthearted music)

00:00:34.192 --> 00:00:37.359
(fast exciting music)

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.730
- My name is Zelda Fassler.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:44.300
I'm a resident of the Hebrew Home.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.200
I've been working with the HOPE class

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.570
since just about two
months after I got here.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:53.610
- [Teacher] What kind of
feelings do you guys get

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.740
from this painting over here?

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.200
- The whole program is very unique

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.100
because it's a high school
within a nursing home facility.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.570
You guys can just turn to the second page.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.270
The whole program is a vocational program

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.850
that started back in the '90s,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.600
that gives students with
intellectual disabilities

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.120
the opportunity to
split their time between

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.580
being in their different departments,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.903
their academic studies.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:20.210
And then working with the residents

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.890
and interact with them on a daily basis.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.210
I think it's a win win
for both the residents

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.130
and the students.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.680
They share ideas, past experiences,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.683
and gain different perspectives
on how life is today.

00:01:33.712 --> 00:01:34.800
(playful music)

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.800
- I feel that most of them
are like grandchildren to me.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.700
I see them around the
home, we stop, we talk.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.643
Some of them knock on my door.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.930
Wanda, she'll just come in for a hug.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.800
The twins come in for a hug.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.373
It's a lovely feeling.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.653
The thrifty social worker.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.610
I'm lucky to have that.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.450
And the longer we're
together, the closer we get.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:27.060
And the more they look
to me as a grandparent,

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.512
I think they think of me in that way,

00:02:30.512 --> 00:02:34.580
because I never act like a teacher.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.550
I'm there to help them,
to explain things to them.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.670
To be his executor.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:41.503
- Oh.

00:02:41.503 --> 00:02:42.418
- Not executer.

00:02:42.418 --> 00:02:43.251
(laughing)

00:02:43.251 --> 00:02:44.500
(playful music)

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.040
It's what keeps my mind fresh;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.370
it's what keeps me feeling young.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:54.190
People say you move into a nursing home

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.880
and that's it.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:00.880
But the HOPE class gives
my life here meaning.

